## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP on partitioning with a minimax objective, a practical budgeting scenario.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions; - Recurrence: min over j of max of subproblem and block sum; - Reconstruction via parent pointers.

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch
function partitionMinMaxSum(a, k) {
  const n = a.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+a[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=pref[i+1];
  for (let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for (let i=0;i<n;i++){
      for (let j=0;j<i;j++){
        const val = Math.max(dp[j][t-1], pref[i+1]-pref[j+0]);
        if (val<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n-1][Math.min(k,n)], cuts: par};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement a monotone-queue or divide-and-conquer optimization here?
- How would you adapt for exactly k vs at most k blocks and output exact cut points?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a DP with a non-trivial cost function and prefix optimization.

## Key Concepts
- DP on prefixes and partitions
- O(1) substring cost via precomputed diff/pref
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
// Precompute diff and prefix
let diff = Array(n+1).fill(0);
for (let i=2;i<=n;i++) diff[i] = s[i-1] !== s[i-2] ? 1:0;
let pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
for (let i=2;i<=n;i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + diff[i];

// cost(a,b)
function cost(a,b){ return pref[b] - pref[a]; }

// DP
let dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
let par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){ dp[i][1] = cost(1,i); }

for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
  for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
    for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
      let val = dp[p][t-1] + cost(p+1,i);
      if(val < dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
    }
  }
}
```

