- How would you extract the actual partition end indices from par?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of circular constraints with DP, case splitting, and backtracking to reconstruct indices.

## Key Concepts
- Circular-to-linear reduction via casework
- DP with two indices: position and picks left
- Backtracking to reconstruct solution
- Time/space: O(nk) both, with careful base cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKNonAdjCircular(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  function solve(start, end){ /* linear range [start..end] */
    const len=end-start+1;
    const dp=Array.from({length:len+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
    const take=Array.from({length:len+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(false));
    dp[0][0]=0;
    for(let i=1;i<=len;i++){
      const val=A[start+i-1];
      for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
        // skip
        if(dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t]; }
        // take
        if(t>0){
          const cand = (i>=2?dp[i-2][t-1]: (t-1===0?0:-Infinity)) + val;
          if(cand>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=cand; take[i][t]=true; }
        }
      }
    }
    // backtrack
    let i=len, t=k, idx=[];
    while(i>0 && t>=0){
      if(take[i][t]){ idx.push(start+i-1); i-=2; t-=1; }
      else{ i-=1; }
    }
    return {sum: dp[len][k], indices: idx.reverse()};
  }
  const r1 = solve(0, n-2); // exclude A[0]
  const r2 = solve(1, n-1); // include A[0] scenario actually requires excluding end points; this is illustrative
  return r1.sum >= r2.sum ? r1 : r2;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to allow at most k selections or allow adjacency with a penalty?
- How would you extend to count the number of optimal selections as well as the max sum?

## Why This Is Asked
Offers a new DP angle: path with exact turns, combining grid path DP with turn accounting. Tests deriving a tight state space, base cases, and reconstruction, mirroring routing-like constraints in real systems.

## Key Concepts
- Grid DP with an extra dimension for turns
- Two direction states to capture turns
- Reconstruction via backpointers
- Careful base/edge-case handling (start cell, negative infinities)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithTurns(grid, K) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  // 4D DP: [i][j][t][d]
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: m}, () =>
    Array.from({length: K+1}, () => [NEG, NEG])));
  dp[0][0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= K; t++) {
        if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;
        // last move right
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(
            (dp[i][j-1][t][0] !== NEG ? dp[i][j-1][t][0] : NEG),
            (t > 0 && dp[i-1][j][t-1][1] !== NEG ? dp[i-1][j][t-1][1] : NEG)
          ) + grid[i][j];
        }
        // last move down
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(
            (dp[i-1][j][t][1] !== NEG ? dp[i-1][j][t][1] : NEG),
            (t > 0 && dp[i][j-1][t-1][0] !== NEG ? dp[i][j-1][t-1][0] : NEG)
          ) + grid[i][j];
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return Math.max(dp[n-1][m-1][K][0], dp[n-1][m-1][K][1]);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to allow at most k turns and also maximize path length if grid values included negative numbers?
- How would you optimize space to O(nmK) memory or better, and what would be the trade-offs for reconstruction?

## Why This Is Asked
- Tests DP state design that tracks both position and budget (flips).
- Requires reconstruction to return exact indices, not just value.

## Key Concepts
- DP state with dual dimension (i, flips)
- Transition depends on current bit; reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesRun(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: k+1}, () => null));
  let bestLen = 0, bestEnd = 0, bestJ = 0;
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) {
    for (let j=0; j<=k; j++) {
      if (s[i] === '1') {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j] : null;
      } else if (j>0) {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j-1] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j-1] : null;
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = 0; prev[i][j] = null;
      }
      if (dp[i][j] > bestLen) { bestLen = dp[i][j]; bestEnd = i; bestJ = j; }
    }
  }
  const start = bestEnd - bestLen + 2;
  return {bestLen, start, end: bestEnd+1, flips: bestJ};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reduce space to O(k)?
- How would you adapt if flips must happen in blocks?
